# Lint toolchain pin (Phase 10 / D-18). CI installs SwiftFormat and SwiftLint with `brew install`,
# which is UNPINNED: without this file, the violation count on a runner is whatever Homebrew ships
# that day, and a remediation measured under one version gated by another is not a remediation.
# Tools/scripts/toolchain-policy.sh asserts the installed versions match these, and FAILS LOUDLY
# rather than silently accepting drift. Bumping a version here is a DELIBERATE act: re-run the
# sweep under the new version, update the committed baseline, then update this pin, in one commit.
#
# Measured on the sweep machine (Apple M5 Pro, macOS 26.5) on 2026-09-07 with
# `swiftformat --version` and `swiftlint version`.
#
# BUMPED 2026-09-07, after the first CI run, in the order this gate's error message prescribes:
# re-measure first, then pin. The first run on macos-15 failed here because Homebrew shipped
# swiftformat 0.63.0 and swiftlint 0.65.1 while this file pinned 0.61.1 / 0.63.3, which is exactly
# the drift the gate exists to catch. Both tools were upgraded locally to the runner's versions and
# the sweep RE-RUN before these numbers moved:
#
#   swiftlint 0.65.1   --strict -> 0 violations, unchanged from 0.63.3.
#   swiftformat 0.63.0 --lint   -> 70 sites in 20 files, all from ONE new default rule,
#                                  wrapIfStatementBodies. Applied, not disabled: it is cosmetic,
#                                  changes no semantics, and the alternative was a third documented
#                                  --disable in .swiftformat with no substantive objection behind
#                                  it. +122/-45 lines; no committed JSON or *-evidence.md changed;
#                                  12 policy gates, 44/32/19 Swift tests and 289 pytest all green
#                                  after.
#
# The Phase-10 baseline in .planning/phases/10-v1-real-data-closed-loop-launch/10-lint-baseline.md
# was taken under 0.61.1 / 0.63.3 and is superseded for the tool versions by this bump; its
# violation counts still describe the pre-sweep repo.
SWIFTFORMAT_VERSION=0.63.0
SWIFTLINT_VERSION=0.65.1
